<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48433" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĭthymălus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĭthymallus</span></b> ), i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιθύμαλος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a plant with a
				milklike sap</i>, <i>spurge</i> (Euphorbia,
			Linn.), of many species, <i><span class="en">Plin. 26, 8, 39, § 62</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 108</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Ser. Samm. 46, 841</span></i>; <i><span class="en">64,
				1106</span></i>.—A female species, called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĭthymălis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>sea-spurge</i>:
			Euphorbia paralias, Linn.; <i><span class="en">Plin. 26, 8, 41, §
		68</span></i>.</div>
